## What is redistributed

The two small uploaded archives are included unchanged so the baseline and original Theory verifier can be reproduced offline. Selected current/earlier manuscript sources and PDFs are copied unchanged into `CONTEXT_SNAPSHOTS/`, with an explicit source mapping. The large recovered research and compiler archives are not duplicated in full; they remain identified by their Library-derived filenames and hashes. This keeps the package compact without pretending to reproduce every portfolio experiment.

All shared Draft 3 files in B and P were compared by SHA-256; the result is recorded in `draft3_source_comparison.json`. The missing small-handoff bibliography input is available in `CONTEXT_SNAPSHOTS/structural_v3/references_formatted.tex`. No revised author manuscript has been synthesized by this audit.

## Evidence generated by this audit

`clean_correctness_replay.json` is the faithful eight-process replay receipt. `benchmark_audit_replay.json` is the full new timing output, not the older supplied times. `theory_original_replay.json` records the original Theory verifier output. `independent_math_audit.py` and `independent_math_results.json` are the separately authored new validation. `benchmark_case_summary.csv` and `execution_summary.json` aggregate the actual results.

The observer wrapper records historical absolute paths from this execution and is not the recommended portable runner. Use the top-level `reproduce.py` instead. Portability-check receipts, if present, refer to a path-only adaptation of the original Theory verifier and are not a substitute for the recorded unmodified replay.

Integrity checks: B manifest 523 entries, P manifest 630 entries, both PASS. Correctness source hashes and non-timing outputs match the original baseline. These facts are machine-checkable in the included JSON receipts.
